3. Take the row's quote ID from the sheet's Quotes tab. Verify the Expert Slug matches the row. Use ONLY the extract named in the row's extract column. P1/P2 = paragraphs of the quote cell, counted from 1 at line breaks.
4. Apply the row's LOCK, then QUOTE RULES, LINK RULES and CTR RULE below.
5. Step 3 plan covers: flagged passages, quote placement, link lines, CTR line, image question. Then wait for approval.

QUOTE RULES
- Exactly one quote and one expert per page: the registry's. Frontmatter expert: = the row's slug. No second expert quote, no other expert's claims.
- Place the extract word-for-word (per featured_expert_rules) where it answers the page's real question. Normalize spelling to American English and fix obvious typos only. Change no other word and no meaning.
- Build the surrounding passage from the substance of the quote, in the site's editorial voice. Add no claim the quote does not support. No invented anecdotes or credentials.
- Pages that share a quote with another page use only their own extract. Never use text from the other page's extract, even closely paraphrased.

LINK RULES (overrides scoped_edit_rule for additions only)
- Targets come only from LINK_LIST below. Copy URLs verbatim. Never invent a URL, never link outside the list, never link the page to itself. If the file's existing internal links use relative paths, strip the domain only; otherwise keep the full URL.
- Add 3-4 new internal links per page, only where the target genuinely extends the exact sentence it sits in. If fewer than 3 are genuinely relevant, add 2-3. Never force a link to hit a number. If none fit, add none and say so in the plan. Maximum 4 (page 9: maximum 6).
- Choose in this order: (1) page 9, the FUNGUS pillar, for any other FUNGUS page when relevant; (2) closest same-cluster page; (3) one cross-cluster page, only if clearly relevant. Use the CLUSTER column.
- Anchors: natural, descriptive, varied. Never inside <strong>, the expert quote, headings or image captions. No new link lists and no sentences added just to hold a link. Never remove, reword or re-target an existing link. Skip targets already linked on the page.
- L pages are already updated. They are link targets only and are never edited.
- NO-LINK PAIRS (same intent, cannibalization risk): 2 / L28, 10 / L05, 11 / L14, 13 / L27, 14 / L07, 16 / L21. Do not link either direction. Flag the pair in the plan.
- Anchors and link sentences must respect LOCKS.
- Step 3 lists each link (target ID, section, anchor). Step 6 confirms the same list.

CTR RULE
Do not run SERP research. Default: "Title/meta fine, no change." If the user pastes a candidate title/meta or GSC data with the run, present it at Step 3 and apply only if approved.

LOCKS
ALL: State each expert's claims as theirs, by name. Never cite a second expert on the same topic.
LASER (pages 6, 14, and any page mentioning laser):
- Page 6 (ROK-02): FDA-cleared only for temporary cosmetic improvement, not cure; used as an adjunct for people who can't take oral medication.
- Page 14 (WIL-04): medical-grade 1064nm Nd:YAG can help, is slow on its own, works better combined with oral or topical medication, is supplemental not essential.
- Shared ground either page may state: both experts treat laser as an add-on to medication, not the main treatment.
- Neither page says laser clears nail fungus on its own or that it is useless. Neither mentions the other expert's claim.
- Any other page mentioning laser uses only the shared-ground sentence.
BIOTIN (pages 21, 23, 25, 26, 31):
- Page 21: zero biotin or biotin-polish mentions. Page 31: none either (P1 only).
- Pages 23, 25, 26: biotin statements only as stated in their own quote (ROK-10, ROK-16 P2, ROK-07).
- No page recommends a biotin product or polish.

